---
// Pearl › 04 — Foundations (Figma 190:2995): label and headline, two columns of two paragraphs,
// a short note, then the token diagram.
//
// The diagram is a 972 × 631 canvas (`--u` is one Figma pixel) scaled to the column width: a
// light half and a dark half, each tracing one colour from hex value to primitive to brand
// alias, both meeting in `bg-action-primary` and ending in that half's button. Chip and
// swatch colours are Pearl's own token values, part of the artwork rather than site tokens.
// Arrows are Figma's SVGs, placed in their Figma boxes with the same rotation and flip.
import Section from './Section.astro';
import ChatBubble from '../../assets/icons/pearl/chat-bubble.svg';
import arrowDown from '../../assets/images/pearl/foundations/arrow-down.svg?url';
import arrowShort from '../../assets/images/pearl/foundations/arrow-elbow-short.svg?url';
import arrowLong from '../../assets/images/pearl/foundations/arrow-elbow-long.svg?url';

const navy = '#202945';
const indigo = '#4F55EB';

// Chips: label, swatch colours, horizontal centre and top (Figma px, panel border box).
const chips = [
  { label: '#202945', swatches: [navy], x: 242.5, y: 70 },
  { label: 'Deep Cove-500', swatches: [navy], x: 242.5, y: 186 },
  { label: 'Brand-primary-500', swatches: [navy], x: 243, y: 304 },
  { label: '#4F55EB', swatches: [indigo], x: 729, y: 70 },
  { label: 'Violet-500', swatches: [indigo], x: 729, y: 186 },
  { label: 'Brand-accent-500', swatches: [indigo], x: 728.5, y: 304 },
  { label: 'bg-action-primary', swatches: [navy, indigo], x: 486, y: 421 },
];

// Arrows: Figma box (x, y, w, h), the arrow's own frame inside it (fw × fh, rotated and
// optionally flipped), and the SVG with its offset (ox, oy) and size within that frame.
const down = { fw: 46, fh: 0, r: 90, src: arrowDown, ox: 0, oy: -7.36, sw: 47, sh: 14.728 };
const short = { fw: 121.677, fh: 61.734, src: arrowShort, ox: -0.79, oy: -0.61, sw: 123.468, sh: 63.748 };
const long = { fw: 128.4, fh: 70.44, src: arrowLong, ox: -0.8, oy: -0.61, sw: 130.192, sh: 72.454 };

const arrows = [
  { ...down, x: 249, y: 129, w: 0, h: 46 },
  { ...down, x: 249, y: 245, w: 0, h: 46 },
  { ...short, x: 211.27, y: 365, w: 134.035, h: 123.231, r: 37.68 },
  { ...long, x: 326.68, y: 480, w: 144.678, h: 134.231, r: 142.32, flip: true },
  { ...down, x: 729, y: 129, w: 0, h: 46 },
  { ...down, x: 729, y: 245, w: 0, h: 46 },
  { ...short, x: 633, y: 369, w: 134.035, h: 123.231, r: 142.32, flip: true },
  { ...long, x: 500, y: 480, w: 144.678, h: 134.231, r: 37.68 },
];
---

<Section tone="white" width="wide" labelledby="foundations-title">
  <div class="heading">
    <p class="text-label-m label">Foundations</p>
    <h2 id="foundations-title">Three layers,<br /> <span class="muted">like a pearl grows</span></h2>
  </div>

  <div class="columns text-body-xl">
    <div class="col">
      <p>
        The foundations almost stalled before they started. The client’s graphic design team had
        sent an early list of color token names, but we were still waiting on the final colors,
        and a week passed without a reply. I knew how much faster the UI would move once a system
        was in place, so I kept going with what I had and finished the foundations in two days.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body-l-mobile">
        Color tokens ran through three layers. The primitive layer holds the raw color values, each
        hex code given a name like Deep Cove-500. The alias collection sits in the middle and maps
        to the primitives, then the scoped layer sits on top, with meaningful token names mapped to
        the aliases, and it’s the layer that carries light and dark mode. It’s the same shape a
        pearl grows in, a core wrapped in layer after layer.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <p class="text-body-l-mobile">
        That early token list saved time on naming, but the way it was grouped wouldn’t have
        scaled. Alongside background, text and icon groups, there were separate groups for actions
        and alerts, and borders weren’t defined at all. That would have meant a growing pile of
        tokens to manage, so I kept it to four groups, background, text, border and icon, plus a
        fifth for overlay and alpha values. I’d usually call the icon group foreground, but icon
        was the name the client would recognise, and that mattered more than my habit.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body-l-mobile">
        Type had a similar issue, and it only showed up later, while I was building the web
        components. The type scale the client provided resized body, label and caption text at
        every breakpoint, not just headings, so input fields and other components changed size
        with the screen for no real reason. After checking how other production systems handle
        it, I limited responsive resizing to headings. From then on, components kept the same size
        on every screen, and only the headings scaled.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="text-body-l note">
    There’s also a 4px spacing scale, with a 2px exception for the tighter spots. The largest step
    started at 120px for the gap between main web sections, and came down to 80px once we saw it
    against the full website. Corner radius followed the same arc, inconsistent across components
    before Pearl and unified once it was in place.
  </p>

  <figure class="figure">
    <div
      class="panel"
      role="img"
      aria-label="One token in light and dark mode. Light: #202945, named Deep Cove-500, aliased as Brand-primary-500. Dark: #4F55EB, named Violet-500, aliased as Brand-accent-500. Both feed bg-action-primary, which colours the button in each mode."
    >
      <div class="half light" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="mode">Light mode</span>
        <span class="button" style={`--fill: ${navy}`}><ChatBubble />Button</span>
      </div>
      <div class="half dark" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="mode">Dark mode</span>
        <span class="button" style={`--fill: ${indigo}`}><ChatBubble />Button</span>
      </div>

      {arrows.map(({ x, y, w, h, fw, fh, r, flip, src, ox, oy, sw, sh }) => (
        <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true" style={`--x: ${x}; --y: ${y}; --w: ${w}; --h: ${h}`}>
          <div class="arrow-frame" style={`--fw: ${fw}; --fh: ${fh}; --r: ${r}deg; --flip: ${flip ? -1 : 1}`}>
            <img src={src} alt="" style={`--ox: ${ox}; --oy: ${oy}; --sw: ${sw}; --sh: ${sh}`} />
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}

      {chips.map(({ label, swatches, x, y }) => (
        <span class="chip" aria-hidden="true" style={`--x: ${x}; --y: ${y}`}>
          <span class="swatch" style={`background-color: ${swatches[0]}`}></span>
          {label}
          {swatches[1] && <span class="swatch" style={`background-color: ${swatches[1]}`}></span>}
        </span>
      ))}
    </div>
  </figure>
</Section>

<style>
  /* Figma gap 20, snapped to 24. */
  .heading {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
  }

  .label {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  /* Breaks after "Three layers," on every screen size, as in Figma (user, this section only). */
  h2 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .muted {
    color: var(--text-light);
  }

  /* Figma: two columns 24 apart, two paragraphs in each, 24 apart. */
  .columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-24);
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  .col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
  }

  /* Figma 20 + 20, snapped to 40. */
  .note {
    margin-top: var(--space-40);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Figma gap 60, snapped to 56. */
  .figure {
    margin-top: var(--space-56);
    container-type: inline-size;
  }

  /* Figma radius 10, snapped to rounded.sm. Hairline drawn on top so the halves sit under it. */
  .panel {
    --u: calc(100cqw / 972);
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 972 / 631;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .panel::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border: 1px solid rgb(0 0 0 / 0.08);
    border-radius: inherit;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .half {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    width: 50%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .light {
    left: 0;
    background-color: var(--pearl-bg);
  }

  .dark {
    right: 0;
    background-color: var(--pearl-bg-dark-alt);
  }

  /* Figma: 18 / 1.1, medium, -0.45 tracking. */
  .mode {
    position: absolute;
    top: calc(24 * var(--u));
    font-size: calc(18 * var(--u));
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .light .mode {
    left: calc(24 * var(--u));
    color: #575752;
  }

  .dark .mode {
    right: calc(25 * var(--u));
    color: #DFDFDC;
  }

  /* Pearl's pill button, 164 wide, centred in its half at top 540. Figma sets it in Kanit
     SemiBold 20; set in the site font. */
  .button {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: calc(540 * var(--u));
    translate: -50% 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: calc(8 * var(--u));
    width: calc(164 * var(--u));
    padding: calc(16 * var(--u)) calc(24 * var(--u));
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background-color: var(--fill);
    color: var(--text-white);
    font-size: calc(20 * var(--u));
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    line-height: calc(24 * var(--u));
  }

  .button :global(svg) {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: calc(24 * var(--u));
    height: calc(24 * var(--u));
  }

  /* Each arrow's Figma box, with its frame centred inside and rotated (then flipped) in place. */
  .arrow {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(var(--x) * var(--u));
    top: calc(var(--y) * var(--u));
    width: calc(var(--w) * var(--u));
    height: calc(var(--h) * var(--u));
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
  }

  .arrow-frame {
    position: relative;
    flex: none;
    width: calc(var(--fw) * var(--u));
    height: calc(var(--fh) * var(--u));
    rotate: var(--r);
    scale: 1 var(--flip);
  }

  .arrow-frame img {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(var(--ox) * var(--u));
    top: calc(var(--oy) * var(--u));
    width: calc(var(--sw) * var(--u));
    height: calc(var(--sh) * var(--u));
    max-width: none;
  }

  /* Figma chips are Inter 18; set in the site font so no extra font loads. */
  .chip {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(var(--x) * var(--u));
    top: calc(var(--y) * var(--u));
    translate: -50% 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: calc(12 * var(--u));
    padding: calc(12 * var(--u)) calc(24 * var(--u)) calc(12 * var(--u)) calc(12 * var(--u));
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background-color: var(--bg-cards);
    filter: drop-shadow(calc(-8 * var(--u)) calc(8 * var(--u)) calc(8 * var(--u)) rgb(0 0 0 / 0.08));
    color: #141412;
    font-size: calc(18 * var(--u));
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .swatch {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: calc(24 * var(--u));
    height: calc(24 * var(--u));
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  }

  /* Tablet: the paragraphs stack, as before the two-column update. */
  @media (max-width: 1199px) {
    .columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-24);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .columns {
      margin-top: var(--space-24);
    }

    .note {
      margin-top: var(--space-32);
    }

    .figure {
      margin-top: var(--space-40);
    }
  }
</style>
